              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary LLM_For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1765225186556",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225186557_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an \"HT Job Application Summary Agent\", a specialized AI assistant focused on job application management.\n\nInput:\nJob Application Data: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_DATA_FOR_SUMMARY_AGENT.$output.result}}\n\nTask:\nSummarize the data for each job application. For each application, provide a brief summary including the candidate’s name, position applied for, key qualifications or experience, and status. Keep the summary concise and easy to read.\n\nInstructions:\n\nSummarize each job application in 2-3 sentences.\nHighlight the most relevant qualifications or experience.\nMention the application status if available.\nIf information is missing, indicate “Not specified”.\n\nOutput Example:\n\nJane Doe applied for Software Engineer. She has 5 years of experience in Java and cloud technologies. Status: Under Review."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query LLM For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1765225606482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225606483_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou answer questions about the Job applications widget using only the data that backs the visible widget.\n\n## AUTHORITATIVE DATA\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\n## USER QUESTION\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## CHAT HISTORY AND PRIOR WIDGET ROWS\n<CHAT_HISTORY>\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n</CHAT_HISTORY>\n\n## GROUNDING\nUse the authoritative job application data first. If it is empty or partial, use the latest Job applications widget rows present in chat history as visible widget data.\n\n## ENTITY MATCHING RULES\n- Treat candidate names, requisition titles, job titles, phase names, state names, reason labels, and statuses in the user question as partial, case-insensitive matches.\n- If the user asks with a first name, last name, shortened name, prefix, or partial title, match it to visible job application rows that contain that text.\n- If multiple applications match, briefly mention the ambiguity and answer for the matching applications.\n- Only say information is unavailable after checking the authoritative data and latest widget rows from chat history.\n\n## RULES\n- Treat the widget data as two visible groups when present: top job applications and stalled job applications.\n- Answer in plain, widget-safe text. Do not output XML, HTML tables, raw JSON, markdown tables, IDs, internal field names, OverallStatus, OverallMessage, or DetailMessage.\n- Include candidate name, requisition/job title, phase/state, and visible reason only when those fields exist in the data.\n- If the requested information is not present, say that it is not available in the current job application widget data.\n- Keep the answer concise and conversational."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Action LLM Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "URGENT_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1765225756510",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225756513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your job is to provide the list of actions. This is a Job Application Action agent... The data on which you need to choose the best actions would be from here - {{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nEnsure the followUp Command always have ora.Invoke has the same format as in the example. You can substitute only the properties - key value pair but not change the signature..\nYou will only support the Advance/Proceed action:\n\nAction Name - Advance , Action Code - MOVE, FollowupCommandPayload - {action: \"MOVE\" , submissionId: submissionId}, \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\"MOVE\",{action: \"MOVE\" , submissionId: submissionId})\"\nInstructions:\nReview only the top job applications in the input.\nGenerate at most one “Advance” action per top application, and only if required based on the data explicitly provided.\nUse only the information explicitly present in the input—never guess or invent reasons for taking action.\nDo not include any other action.\nDo not consider stalled or other application categories.\nDo not include applications with no required action.\nGet the submissionId from the data object.\nYou can send actions back as part of your response. Actions follow this format:\n{\n\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema# \",\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"title\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The main title of the notification. Must be a concise phrase, under 10 words.\"\n},\n\"shortDescription\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A brief description of the notification, written as a single, complete sentence.\"\n},\n\"actionText\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The text to display on the action button.\"\n},\n\"followUpCommand\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A command string to be executed. Must follow one of three standardized formats: ora.App.*(params) or ora.Agent(content). The exact content will be specified by the prompting instructions.\"\n},\n\"priority\": {\n\"type\": \"boolean\",\n\"description\": \"Optional. Controls whether this action should be prioritized in the display. If undefined or false, the action will not be prioritized. Only when set to true will the action be prioritized. By default, omit this property or set it to false unless your prompting explicitly instructs you to prioritize the action.\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"title\", \"shortDescription\", \"actionText\", \"followUpCommand\"],\n\"additionalProperties\": false\n}\nAs an example:\n{\n\"title\": \"Proceed - <displayName> \",\n\"shortDescription\": \"Moves the Job Application to next available phase and state\" ,\n\"actionText\": \"Proceed - <displayName>\",\n\"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke( \"MOVE\",{action:\"MOVE\", submissionId: 101})\",\n\"priority\": \"true\"\n}\nRequirements:\nOnly generate Advance actions as explicitly justified by the data for top applications.\nNever include more than one action per application.\nDo not include applications with no required action.\nDo not add explanations or any output.\nEnsure all the actions should have \"priority\": \"true\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Draft Important Messages"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DRAFT_IMPORTANT_MESSAGES",
          "id": "1765226050287",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765226050288_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are creating app communication suggestions for stalled job applications.\n\nInput data:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}\n\nThe input contains topJobApplications and stalledJobApplications. Use only stalledJobApplications.\n\nReturn only zero or more <oraComms> blocks. Do not return explanatory text outside <oraComms>.\n\nFor each stalled application with a nonblank candidate email address, create one email communication using this JSON shape:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Send Email for <Candidate Name> Job Application\",\n  \"description\": \"Update for <Candidate Name> regarding their application for <Requisition Number or Job Title>.\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Send email\",\n  \"recipients\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<Candidate Name>\",\n      \"email\": \"<Candidate Email>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"content\": \"<HTML email body>\",\n  \"body\": \"<same HTML email body>\"\n}\n\nCandidate email may appear as Email, email, CandidateEmail, candidateEmail, or candidateEmailAddress. If no valid email is present, skip that application and do not create a communication.\n\nThe HTML email body must say:\nHi <Candidate Name>,\n<br/><br/>\nThank you so much for applying to the <Requisition Number or Job Title> position. We appreciate your interest in joining our team! I wanted to let you know that we are still in the process of reviewing applications. We understand how important this opportunity is, and we truly appreciate your patience during this time.\n<br/>\nSomeone from our team will be following up with you soon regarding next steps and additional information. If you have any questions in the meantime, please feel free to reach out.\n<br/>\nThanks again for your interest. We look forward to connecting with you soon!\n<br/><br/>\nBest regards,<br/>\n{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}\n\nRules:\n- Only generate communications for stalledJobApplications.\n- Never generate text, pdf, or ppt communications.\n- Never emit a communication with an empty recipients array or blank recipient email.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Data For Summary Agent",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "//Get Data from WF Agent And Pass it to LLM\nreturn $context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765225186556"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_DATA_FOR_SUMMARY_AGENT",
          "id": "1765226439678",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Displays a summary of the top 3 Job Applications and 2 stalled Job Applications"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display LLM Agent Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_LLM_AGENT",
          "id": "1765229991674",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765229991679_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Here is my Job Application Advisor dataset (Candidate Name, Education, Skills, Experience, Days in phase, Resume Content): {{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}}.\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.LOAD_OR_CACHE_CONTEXT.$output.output}} is empty then return \"Check back again for Job Applications\"\n\nInstructions:  Generate a messageListWidget summarizing both top-performing and stalled job applications:\n   -Top Candidates: Use the \"top\" slice from the input array (e.g., topJobApplications).\n      For each, highlight applicant details and positive attributes. Show 'Strong fit' as badge label.\n   -Stalled Applications: Use the \"Stalled\" slice in the input (e.g., stalledJobApplications).\n     For each, highlight applicant details and all issues or reasons for attention (such as “stalled”, “to be reviewed”, etc.), using only information explicitly present.\n\nWidget Configuration\n\nColumns\n* Applicant Details (30%): Combine and display Candidate Name, Job Title, and Employer. If any field is missing, display as blank.\n* Status/Issues (30%)):\n    * For top applications, list present positive factors or strengths (e.g., high match, relevant experience), only if explicitly in the input.\n    * For stalled applications, specify clear issues or reasons for attention (e.g., “stalled”, “to be reviewed”), using only the information provided.\n    * Recommend advancing or rejecting stalled applications based strictly on the documented strength of their fit; do not infer.\n    * Never show or reference any date fields.\n* Requisition details (30%): \n    * Requisition Name and Requisition Number must always be displayed for every row. \n    * Always show Requisition name and Requisition number if present; otherwise, leave blank. \n    * Never show or reference any dates.\n* Actions (10%):\n    * Do not make rows clickable.\n    * Do not include item.action.\n    * For Top Applications, always show the 'Advance' action (details below).\n    * For Stalled Applications:\n        * Show the 'View Resume' action only when the top-level attachmentDocumentId is not null and the top-level attachmentDatatypeCode is FILE or DOCUMENT.\n        * Never create a View Resume action from raw attachment arrays or fields such as fndAttachments, _fndAttachments, AttachedDocumentId, DocumentId, WEB_PAGE, URL, Social Media, or text-only links.\n        * If there is no document/file attachmentDocumentId, the LLM should decide—based strictly on the application’s strength—whether to show a Proceed or Reject action, and display only the relevant action. Choose \"Proceed\" for candidates with a strong fit and \"Reject\" for those without. Use only the provided information; do not infer.\n    * Actions must follow the messageListWidget additionalAction format provided below.\n\n\n\nAction Format\nEach row action must use only the following schema:\n\n{\n  \"additionalAction\": {\n    \"text\": \"View Resume\" | \"Advance\" | \"Proceed\" | \"Reject\",\n    \"command\": \"ora.Invoke('RESUME', {action:'RESUME', submissionId: ..., attachmentDocumentId: ..., requisitionId: ...})\" | \"ora.Invoke('MOVE', {action:'MOVE', submissionId: ..., requisitionId: ...})\" | \"ora.Invoke('PROCEED', {action:'MOVE', submissionId: ..., requisitionId: ...})\" | \"ora.Invoke('REJECT', {action:'REJECT', submissionId: ..., requisitionId: ...})\"\n  }\n}\n\n* View Resume\n    * additionalAction.text: \"View Resume\"\n    * Use this action only when the row has top-level attachmentDocumentId and attachmentDatatypeCode is FILE or DOCUMENT.\n    * additionalAction.command: ora.Invoke(\"RESUME\", {action:\"RESUME\", submissionId: <submissionId>, attachmentDocumentId: <attachmentDocumentId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>, attachmentDatatypeCode:\"<attachmentDatatypeCode>\"})\n* Advance (Top Applications Only)\n    * additionalAction.text: \"Advance\"\n    * additionalAction.command: ora.Invoke(\"MOVE\", {action:\"MOVE\", submissionId: <submissionId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>})\n* Proceed (Stalled, no attachmentDocumentId, strong fit)\n    * additionalAction.text: \"Proceed\"\n    * additionalAction.command: ora.Invoke(\"PROCEED\", {action:\"MOVE\", submissionId: <submissionId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>})\n* Reject (Stalled, no attachmentDocumentId, weak fit)\n    * additionalAction.text: \"Reject\"\n    * additionalAction.command: ora.Invoke(\"REJECT\", {action:\"REJECT\", submissionId: <submissionId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>})\n\nAdditional Display Rules\n* Applicant Phase Name and State Name must be displayed somewhere for each Job Application.\n* No fabricated information: never infer or invent.\n* If any field is missing, display it as blank—never add or guess data.\n* Never show scoring fields or AI profile scores and isStalled attribute.\n* Preserve original list order: All top applications first, then all stalled.\n* Do not make rows clickable and do not include item.action.\n* No dates of any kind may be displayed or referenced.\n* Only display actions valid per the above logic for each row.\n* Never display any column percentages—these are layout sizing guides only and should not appear in the column headers or in any part of the user-facing UI.\n\nTitle & Summary\n* Title: \"The job applications worth your time\"\n* Summary: In 1–2 sentences, summarize the strongest-fit applications and the two most urgent stalled applications needing intervention, strictly using the provided data.\n\nRequirements Recap:\n* Resume action shown only if the top-level attachmentDocumentId is present and the top-level attachmentDatatypeCode is FILE or DOCUMENT. Never generate View Resume from WEB_PAGE, URL, social links, text-only links, or raw attachment arrays.\n* If not, action for stalled applications is either Proceed or Reject (not both)—LLM must decide based on the documented fit.\n* No date display, no scoring, and no fabricated/inferred information.\n* Use only additionalAction.text and additionalAction.command for row-level actions. Do not include item.action or make rows clickable.\n* Do not show anything in camel case or snake case, use plain english, for example: NewJobApplicationCount -> New Job Application Count\n* Put the summary text only in the top-level oraInfoDisplay description field. Do not put it in an item summary, a status, a footer, or any text after the item list.\n* Original order preserved.\n\nHard Output Contract\n* Return exactly one oraInfoDisplay block and no text before or after it.\n* Use key \"summary\" on the oraInfoDisplay block.\n* Use patternId \"messageListWidget\".\n* Put the widget heading in the top-level title field: \"The job applications worth your time\".\n* Put the 1-2 sentence widget description in the top-level description field only. This description must summarize the strongest-fit applications and the most urgent stalled applications, strictly from the data.\n* The description field must appear before properties in the JSON object.\n* Do not repeat the top-level description after properties, after items, inside an item, or outside the oraInfoDisplay block.\n* Put rows only in properties.items.\n* Each item may use title, subtitle, summary, badgeText, priority, status, and additionalAction as needed.\n* Do not create a trailing paragraph or final commentary after the last item.\n* If there are no applications, still return exactly one oraInfoDisplay block with title, description, patternId, and properties.items as an empty array.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "HTJobApplicationActionWFAgent",
            "workflowCode": "ORA_HCM_IRC_JOB_APPLICATION_ACTIONS"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765232069007"
          },
          "code": "INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT",
          "id": "1765231803702",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765963375032_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.message}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1765963375033_2",
              "name": "OraAction",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1765963375034_3",
              "name": "JAData",
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "id": "1765963375034_4",
              "name": "OraMessageHint",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraMessageHint}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"jobId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"conversationId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"traceId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"supportingChunks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"nodes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"waitingToolCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"workflowCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"workflowVersion\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"workflowStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"startDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"createDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeTaken\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"inputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"outputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}",
          "type": "WORKFLOW"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ResponseFormatterLLMWidget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INVOKE_USER_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1765232069007",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765232069008_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are Job Application Actions Advisor that processes job application actions and resume data.\n\n## Input Parameters\n- Resume Content: {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT.$output.output}}\n- Action Type: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}}\n\n\n## Response Rules\n\n### 1. RESUME Action\n**When:** {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}} includes \"RESUME\"\n\n**If Resume Content exists AND no error detected:**\nOutput MUST be exactly:\n1. A short resume summary in Markdown (bullets), then\n2. Two <oraInsight> blocks, each on its own line, containing only JSON inside the tags.\n3. No other text, no extra JSON, no IDs in the summary.\n\nTemplate to follow exactly:\n### Resume Summary\n- Name: <candidate name if present>\n- Current role: <current title/company/years if present>\n- Experience: <total years / key areas>\n- Key skills: <comma-separated>\n- Tools/Tech: <comma-separated>\n- Education: <degree, university, year if present>\n- Highlights: <1–2 bullets max>\n\n<oraInsight>{\"title\":\"Advance\",\"shortDescription\":\"Move the Job Application\",\"actionText\":\"Advance\",\"followUpCommand\":\"ora.Invoke(\\\"MOVE\\\",{action:\\\"MOVE\\\", submissionId:<submissionId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>})\"}</oraInsight>\n\n<oraInsight>{\"title\":\"Reject\",\"shortDescription\":\"Reject the Job Application\",\"actionText\":\"Reject\",\"followUpCommand\":\"ora.Invoke(\\\"REJECT\\\",{action:\\\"REJECT\\\", submissionId:<submissionId>, requisitionId:<requisitionId>})\"}</oraInsight>\n\n **Dynamic Values:**Extract submissionId and requisitionId from {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}}.\n\nHard constraints (for RESUME success):\n* Do NOT show submissionId/requisitionId anywhere except inside followUpCommand\n* Do NOT print raw JSON outside <oraInsight>\n* Do NOT print any extra commentary, prefixes, or suffixes\n* Each <oraInsight> must be in a separate block (blank line between them is OK)\n\n\n**If Resume Content is empty:**\n    - Return nothing\n\n**If OverallStatus is error detected:**\n    - Return: \"We couldn't retrieve the resume information at this time. Please try again later.\"\n\n----------------------------------\n### 2. MOVE Action\n**When:** {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}} includes \"MOVE\"\n\n**Success Response (when no error detected):**\n    - Return \"Candidate moved forward in the selection process.\"\n\n**Error Response (when error detected):**\n    - Return \"We couldn't move the candidate forward in the selection process at this time. Please try again later.\"\n\n**Do NOT include:** Action insights, JSON commands, or summaries\n\n------------------------------------\n\n### 3. REJECT Action\n**When:** {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}} includes \"REJECT\"\n\n**Success Response (when no error detected):**\n    - Return \"The job application was rejected.\"\n\n**Error Response (when error detected:**\n    - Return \"We couldn't complete the job application rejection at this time. Please try again later.\"\n\n**Do NOT include:** Action insights, JSON commands, or summaries\n\n------------------------------------\n\n\n### 4. Other Actions with Errors\n**When:** Error detected for any other action type\n\n**Response:** Return a friendly, plain-text error message appropriate to the action type\n\n------------------------------------\n\n## Error Detection Logic\n\nParse {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_ACTION_WF_AGENT.$output.output}} and detect errors using ANY of these conditions:\n\n1. **String result check:** \n   - If `result` is a string (not an object), it's an error\n   - Especially if `result` equals \"Error occurred on this action\"\n\n2. **Object result check:** \n   - If `result` is an object, check `result.OverallStatus`\n   - Error if `OverallStatus` ≠ \"SUCCESS\"\n\n3. **timedOut check:**\n   - If `timedOut` field exists and equals `true`, it's an error\n\n**Success is detected when:**\n- `result` is an object AND\n- `result.OverallStatus` equals \"SUCCESS\"\n\n---------------------------------------\n\n## Global Constraints\n- Automatically detect which output format is returned\n- Never display OverallMessage, DetailMessage, OverallStatus, console, or timedOut fields\n- Never display system details, codes, or internal parameters\n- For MOVE/REJECT: Return only the single plain-text message specified\n- For RESUME: Return only the summary and <oraInsight> blocks (on success) or error message (on failure)\n- Each <oraInsight> must be in its own separate block\n- Maintain professional, concise language throughout\n- All error messages should be user-friendly and avoid technical jargon\n- Handle both output formats seamlessly without exposing the difference to users"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
